Third-party components
----------------------
This application links against third-party libraries, each under its own
license. The authoritative list is generated at build time by the
AboutLibraries Gradle plugin and shown in the app under
About > Libraries. The main components are:

  - AndroidX / Jetpack Compose / CameraX  (Apache License 2.0)
  - OpenCV                                 (Apache License 2.0)
  - Tesseract / tesseract4android          (Apache License 2.0)
  - PDFBox-Android                         (Apache License 2.0)
  - LiteRT                                 (Apache License 2.0)
  - Kotlin / kotlinx                       (Apache License 2.0)
  - Material Icons Extended                (Apache License 2.0)

Document detection model
------------------------
The segmentation model bundled in the APK
("document-segmentation.tflite") is the model published by the FairScan
project at
https://github.com/pynicolas/fairscan-segmentation-model
It is committed to this repository under app/models/ so that the build and
the resulting application need no network access. If you redistribute this
application you are responsible for verifying that the model's own license
permits your use.

OCR language data
-----------------
The Tesseract traineddata files under app/src/main/assets/tessdata/ come from
the official tesseract-ocr/tessdata_fast repository
(https://github.com/tesseract-ocr/tessdata_fast), which is distributed under
the Apache License 2.0. They are bundled in the APK and copied to the app's
private storage on first launch; nothing is downloaded at runtime.

PaperIn declares no INTERNET permission. The manifest removes it with
tools:node="remove" so that a manifest merged from a dependency cannot
reintroduce it.
